cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived artifacts, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Provenance Confounding in Image Authenticity Classification:
  code and analysis pipeline
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipeline and manuscript sources for a study of class-conditional
  provenance confounding: when the two classes of an authenticity-classification
  image dataset are sourced by different procedures, the label predicts the
  acquisition process rather than the property being labeled, and no
  in-distribution evaluation can detect it. Contains the data pipeline, four
  model families evaluated without and with an exploratory normalization,
  a balanced external test (46 regulator-confirmed falsified against 46
  authentic-labeled photographs, one ingestion pipeline), an external
  acquisition-shift test on two capture conditions, cluster-bootstrap
  intervals, a label-free normalization operator with per-axis, per-constant
  and per-order ablations, region substitution, a five-seed variance sweep,
  calibration and two independent attribution analyses, and a provenance
  audit run across four application areas. Also contains the Journal of
  Imaging manuscript package (mdpi-jimaging/). Redistributes no dataset
  images apart from CC BY 4.0 Mendeley photographs shown in two figures.
